text:
G19.1 BUILT and pushed (1e3703a). The process spec is written (design/principles/PROCESSES.md). Server processes get their job id and your node's door; spirit.core.ask works from a process; an app's own code runs as its server job ('server': '<file>'). Also in:
- the shutdown verb, sent to every server when your node shuts down;
- Cancel in the jobs app stops servers;
- the monitor gets one line per request and reply, and an error's text always;
- the payload goes to the monitor only for an app marked 'verbose', never node-wide.
Next is G19.2, the passthrough.
